<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Aden</h1><p class="st-meta">1963 CE – 1967 CE · capital Aden</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The former Aden Colony as a member state of the Federation of South Arabia, the scene of the Aden Emergency.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1963 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-aden">Colony of Aden</a> entered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a> as the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, keeping its own government under a chief minister, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> retained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> and control of the military base. The merger was opposed by Aden's nationalists, who resented being joined to the hinterland rulers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden's</a> legislature was elected on a narrow franchise. The chief minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hassan-ali-bayoomi">Hassan Ali Bayoomi</a> supported the merger; a later chief minister, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdul-qawi-mackawee">Abdul Qawi Mackawee</a>, sided with the nationalists and was dismissed in 1965, after which <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> ruled directly. Strikes, bombings and assassinations by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/front-for-the-liberation-of-occupied-south-yemen">FLOSY</a> made Aden the centre of the emergency.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In June 1967 armed nationalists briefly held the Crater district. British forces withdrew in November 1967 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> became the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-aden.jpg" alt="State of Aden" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: EuropeanV · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_State_of_Aden_1963%E2%80%931967.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1963 CE – 1967 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Aden</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hassan Ali Bayoomi, Abdul Qawi Mackawee</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Aden State</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1965&amp;focus=state-of-aden" aria-label="State of Aden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5916 1701 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Aden lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6236 1957L6236 1957M6236 1957L6313 1863M6236 1957L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6236 1957h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6236 1957h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Aden. <a href="/atlas?year=1965&amp;focus=state-of-aden">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
